{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ndefect=json.load(open('update43.json'))['interpretations'][0]\ncorr={\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"98ee8dfd5fac4b84915f91ed4b094bcf-question-0\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_process_config_entry\\\",\\\"src_restore_snapshot_config\\\",\\\"src_newraft_startup\\\",\\\"src_restore_committed\\\"],\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":None,\n \\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Correction account for the enumerated writers of raft's tracked configuration. Source: processConfigurationLogEntry sets the tracked state for LogConfiguration and deprecated peer entries taken from the log and is called by appendEntries for newly appended entries and by the NewRaft startup scan (raft.go:1595-1620, api.go:610-621); appendConfigurationEntry records the configuration the leader appends (raft.go:1238); the conflict path in appendEntries rolls latest back to committed when it deletes a suffix below the latest configuration index (raft.go:1548); restoreSnapshot installs the newest local snapshot's committed configuration and index at startup (api.go:677-678); and installSnapshot installs the metadata of a snapshot received from a leader (raft.go:1960-1961). The FSM's ConfigurationStore is never read back, so an FSM-side copy of the configuration is not a source of the node's decision state. The correction does not weaken any recorded conclusion, and it sharpens the account that prompted it: those conclusions turn on the startup inputs being the snapshot's configuration and the log scan, and on the scan's lower bound, which is exactly what the feature moves; the receipts show the resulting states directly (an empty configuration with a non-zero persisted commit index, the snapshot's older configuration with a zero one, and the recovered configuration when the scan runs).\\\"),\n \\\"answers\\\":{\\\"54dee3b26c0e415f90b11dd070752bc2-gap-9\\\":{\n   \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The corrected statement enumerates the writers: processConfigurationLogEntry for entries taken from the log, appendConfigurationEntry on the leader, the conflict rollback in appendEntries, restoreSnapshot for the local snapshot, and installSnapshot for a streamed one (raft.go:1238, 1548, 1595-1620, 1960-1961; api.go:677-678), with the FSM's ConfigurationStore never read back. Knowledge revision 2 states this, and the interpretation for this question cites it.\\\",\n   \\\"resolved\\\":True}},\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"98ee8dfd5fac4b84915f91ed4b094bcf-knowledge-2\\\",\\\"revision\\\":2,\n   \\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The tracked configuration is written from log entries by processConfigurationLogEntry, by appendConfigurationEntry on the leader, by the conflict rollback in appendEntries, and independently from snapshot metadata by restoreSnapshot and installSnapshot; the FSM's ConfigurationStore is never read back.\\\"}],\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The correction is source-only: no receipt in this run exercises the conflict rollback or the streamed install snapshot path, so those writers are stated from the source rather than observed.\\\",\n  \\\"This account makes no defect judgment; the experiment-cited account for the question remains the defect account.\\\"],\n \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"The enumeration is taken from the call sites of the two setters; a writer reached through an interface or a code path not present in this snapshot would not appear in it.\\\"]}\njson.dump({\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Answers the gap opened by the writer-enumeration correction with a source-only account and re-appends the experiment-cited defect account so the question keeps its defect judgment.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[corr,defect]},open('update44.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update44.json 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"\nimport sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint('valid',d['valid'],'no_change',d.get('no_change'))\nfor x in d.get('diagnostics',[])[:6]: print(x['paths'],x['message'])\nprint([(e['object'],e['action']) for e in d.get('effects',[])])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
